{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.428,
   "text": "The old man who ran the Ferris wheel gave me one rule for closing night."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.028,
   "end": 14.639,
   "text": "If a car ever stops at the very top after the lights go out... don't bring it down."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 15.639,
   "end": 20.055,
   "text": "I laughed. Every car was empty. I'd checked them all myself."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 20.655,
   "end": 24.836,
   "text": "At midnight, I pulled the big switch, and the whole fair went dark."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 25.636,
   "end": 28.623,
   "text": "Then, high above me, something creaked."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 31.223,
   "end": 35.404,
   "text": "One car was rocking at the top. Slow. Back and forth."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.204,
   "end": 40.62,
   "text": "And a small voice drifted down. Please... I want to get off."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 42.02,
   "end": 46.244,
   "text": "I knew the rule. I stood there in the cold for a long time."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 47.844,
   "end": 50.276,
   "text": "But it sounded so scared."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 51.276,
   "end": 55.841,
   "text": "So I pushed the lever. The wheel groaned... and the car came down to me."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 57.041,
   "end": 61.628,
   "text": "Empty. Just the safety bar, still locked... and the seat, still warm."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 62.628,
   "end": 67.855,
   "text": "I climbed in to check under the seat... and the bar slammed shut across my lap."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 69.655,
   "end": 76.353,
   "text": "The wheel began to turn. And far below, at the controls, a little boy in my jacket... waved goodbye."
  }
 ],
